Bosses of Mass Destruction Bedrock
Build: 2.1.28
Status: Development
Minecraft Bedrock: 1.26.40

Current Focus
Obsidilith Performance Hotfix

Primary goal
Fix severe Obsidilith frame drops / crashes reported with Vibrant Visuals without reducing the real combat area or damage coverage.

Obsidilith rift pipeline
Separated gameplay coverage from visual density.
Burst, Wave and Spike still use the complete scanned ground-point set for damage.
Only a bounded representative subset of those points now emits indicator/column particles.
Replaced per-rift/per-layer player queries with one grouped player query per vertical layer.
Removed the extra three radial particle emissions that had been added around every rift layer.
Large attack terrain scanning now probes nearby floor levels first and uses a lower per-tick column budget.

Visual budgets
Burst: maximum 32 visual rifts (149 gameplay cells remain active on a full radius-7 disc).
Wave: maximum 18 visual rifts per stage (all gameplay cells remain active).
Spike: maximum 13 visual rifts, preserving the full radius-2 visual pattern.
Burst/Wave/Spike/Rift particle emitters now create one particle per scripted emission instead of multiplying each call internally.
Anvil trail frequency reduced from every 2 ticks to every 3 ticks.
Anvil impact burst reduced from 70 scripted emissions to 24.
Spike slowness keeps the effect but disables redundant vanilla potion particles.

Estimated particle reduction for the main rift effects
Burst: ~8,493 -> ~256 rendered particles (-97.0%).
Wave: ~2,793 -> ~144 per stage (-94.8%).
Spike: ~1,469 -> ~104 (-92.9%).

Vibrant Visuals / PBR
The hotfix attacks excessive particle count and script-query fan-out rather than disabling the visual pipeline.
